   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "One language, twenty countries",
     "texto": [
      "Speakers from Madrid, Mexico City and Buenos Aires can usually understand one another, but Spanish in the Americas is not one uniform variety. Pronunciation, grammar and vocabulary differ between countries and within them.\n\n**Pronunciation.** **Seseo**, in which c before e or i and z sound like **s**, is widespread in the Americas. Many regions also weaken or omit syllable-final **s**, though this varies by speaker and context.\n\n**Pronouns.** **Ustedes** is the usual plural form across most of the Americas; **vosotros** is not normally used in everyday speech. In some regions, including the Río de la Plata, **vos** replaces **tú** and has forms such as **tenés**, **querés** and **sos**. Other regions use **tú**, **vos** or both, with local patterns.\n\n**Tenses and words.** In many countries, speakers more often use the indefinido with **hoy** than speakers in much of Spain. Everyday words also vary: *coche, carro* and *auto*; *móvil* and *celular*.\n\nThese are broad tendencies, not rules for every speaker. Learning to recognise several varieties makes reading and conversation easier."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Pronouns, tenses and words",
     "texto": [
      "**Spain and the Americas, side by side.**\n\n- vosotros tenéis → **ustedes tienen**\n- tú tienes → **vos tenés** (Río de la Plata and other areas)\n- el coche → **el carro**, **el auto**\n- el móvil → **el celular**\n- el ordenador → **la computadora**\n- conducir → **manejar**\n- el zumo → **el jugo**\n- la patata → **la papa**\n- el billete → **el boleto**\n- aquí → **acá**\n\n**Voseo.** With **vos**, the verb shifts its stress: **tenés**, **querés**, **sos**. The command too: **pasame**, **decime**.\n\n**Hoy.** In Spain the perfect is common: **hoy he comprado**. In many countries of the Americas, the indefinido: **hoy compré**."
     ],
